arily... but we can't mutate record.message? Setting record.message is what formatter does anyway; but requirement says don't rewrite msg/args/exc_info/stack_info. record.message is not in that list, but it's shared and used by handler for other formatters... Actually logging.Formatter.format sets record.message = record.getMessage() on every call, so mutating it is fine-ish but safer not to.\n\nCleanest: create a copy? Requirement said \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\". So we can do:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n    if max_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n        return self._format_full(record)\n    # need to truncate the message only\n```\nWe can temporarily set record.message? Hmm, alternative: build the truncated message and use a temporary wrapper.\n\nImplementation approach: use a shim. Simplest reliable approach:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    message = record.getMessage()\n    truncated = self._truncate(message)\n    if truncated is None:  # unchanged\n        msg = super().format(record)  # normal\n    else:\n        # temporarily replace record.msg/args? Not allowed.\n```\nAlternative: compute the formatted message with the prefix by formatting a subclass? Actually easier: compute prefix manually. super().format uses:\n- record.message = record.getMessage()\n- format string substitution: self._style.format(record) which uses self._fmt % record.__dict__\n- then exc_info/stack_info appended.\n\nWe can do: temporarily set record.message to truncated, call super().format(record), then restore record.message to the original full message. That mutates but restores. Hmm but at end super().format leaves record.message = full; if we restore to original value before our call (which might not exist), fine. Actually doing:\n\n```python\noriginal_message = record.message... \n```\nCareful: during super().format, `record.message = record.getMessage()` gets